> [!NOTE]
> This change is stacked on [#31305](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/31305), which introduces the dense Paged LoRA memory pool. It should be rebased onto the latest Paged LoRA branch and retargeted to `main` after the dependency is merged.

## Motivation

Paged LoRA stores adapter weights in fixed-size rank pages and loads only the pages required by the current batch. However, routed-expert LoRA weights in the classic fused MoE path still use flat, max-rank-padded buffers.

This PR extends Paged LoRA to the classic fused MoE LoRA path. The implementation:

- stores routed-expert LoRA weights in page-backed buffers with an expert dimension;
- passes page tables and per-adapter actual ranks directly to the fused MoE LoRA kernel;
- skips rank blocks beyond the adapter's actual rank;
- supports non-contiguous physical pages and mixed LoRA ranks;
